<p style="margin-top:1em; margin-bottom:0em; page-break-before:always"> </p>
<HR SIZE="3" style="COLOR:#999999" WIDTH="100%" ALIGN="CENTER">


<Center><DIV STYLE="width:8.5in" align="left">

 <P STYLE="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B>DIRECTORS&#8217; REPORT (CONTINUED) </B></P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B>REMUNERATION REPORT (CONTINUED) </B></P> <p STYLE="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt ; font-size:8pt">&nbsp;</P>
 <P STYLE="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B>C. Service agreements </B></P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Remuneration and other terms of employment for executive key management personnel are formalised in service agreements. The service agreements specify the
components of remuneration, benefits, and notice periods. Participating in the STI and LTI plans is subject to the Board&#8217;s discretion. Compensation paid to key management personnel is determined by the CEO and approved by the Board on an
annual basis with reference to market salary surveys. Details of the current terms of these agreements are below. Unless stated otherwise, all salaries quoted below are as at 30&nbsp;June 2026. </P>
<P STYLE="font-size:12pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt">&nbsp;</P>
